cmake: pin every fetched dependency to a full commit

FetchDependencies.cmake names its dependencies by 7-character hash or by
tag, and FetchContent clones them at configure time. A short hash grows
ambiguous as a repository grows, and a tag can be moved, so the same
recipe could build different sources. Each ref is replaced by the full
commit it resolved to on 2026-10-24, the original kept as a comment.
Resolved with `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/commits/<short>` for a hash and
`git ls-remote <url> refs/tags/<tag>^{}` for a tag; all eleven equal the
HEAD of the clone the M7 GENERIC_X64 build fetched (tracy, off in this
build, resolved the same way). The fetch itself still happens at
configure: carrying the sources is #813's follow-up.

